$DIR/main.p:35:6: s1 holds a view of v1 (v1.Slice(), line 32), which was moved to w1 at line 33, so s1 can no longer be used here
    s1 looks at memory that v1 owns, without owning it: the view was made by
    v1.Slice() at line 32. A view of an owner held in a local variable may be
    used only while the variable keeps the value the view was made from. At line
    33 v1 was moved to w1, so the view may look at memory that was released, or
    at a value that now belongs to something else.
    Go keeps memory alive for as long as any pointer refers to it. Plutonium has
    no garbage collector: an owner releases its memory when it is dropped, so a
    view must not be used after the value it looks at has gone.
    Use s1 before line 33, or move v1 only after the last use of s1
    Or move a copy at line 33, so that v1 keeps its value:
        v1.Clone()
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3313" for a longer explanation)

